<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 27.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 27.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended February 27:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   280	   1.17     453750 127.05    21.79</p>
<p>Reliance	     265	   1.12     440850 116.83    22.04</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   190	   0.80     514700  97.79    21.95</p>
<p>ITC		    390	   1.66     218800  85.33    22.19</p>
<p>MTNL		   235	   1.04     233200  54.80    23.08</p>
<p>BSES		   230	   1.00     174450  40.12    22.67</p>
<p>ACC		   1415	   6.13	25720  36.39    22.59</p>
<p>Tata Power	   141	   0.60     251750  35.50    22.19</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    240	   1.04     140800  33.79    22.60</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   900	   3.85	33600  30.24    22.31</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 22.12 percent on an annualised basis against 18.88 percent in the previous carry forward account ended February 22.</p>
